<title>USA: Northern States coal unit down for repair.</title>
<headline>Northern States coal unit down for repair.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern States Power Co said Monday its 176 megawatt Black Dog coal-fired power unit number 4 was taken off line Sunday for tube leak repairs.</p>
<p>No restart date for the Burnsville, Minn., unit has yet been set, Northern States said in a statement.</p>
<p>The unit is one of four at the Black Dog site, which has a total capacity of 461 megawatts.</p>
<p>-- New York Power Desk 212-859-1627</p>
